21. Applying Functions

| Method       | Use                               | Example                                                        |
| ------------ | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `apply()`    | Apply custom function             | `df["Age"].apply(lambda x: x+1)`                               |
| `map()`      | Map values/function on Series     | `df["Gender"].map({"M":"Male","F":"Female"})`                  |
| `applymap()` | Apply function element-by-element | Older approach; use `DataFrame.map()` in newer Pandas versions |


Example:

df["Age"] = df["Age"].apply(lambda x: x + 1)

